    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1105">

                <pb facs="0803" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4229.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following advice of Admiral Mayo based on instructions from Navy Department Vice
                    Consul Bevan and myself came aboard <hi rendition="#italic">Connecticut</hi>
                    yesterday. About twenty Americans remained ashore refusing to leave Tampico.
                    German Consul is looking after Americans during my temporary absence from
                    shore.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
